title:    How the implementation is organised
subtitle: Major directories only. Full source on GitHub.
width:    780
---
week-12-secret-management/
├── LAB.md                      reproduction guide: the global-key constraint, the teardown chain
├── terraform/
│   ├── main.tf                 key, secret, topic, subscription — stage 1
│   └── rotator.tf              the function, gated on deploy_rotator — stage 2
├── rotator/main.py             the rotator Secret Manager does not ship
├── scripts/
│   ├── measure-rotation.py     the load-bearing measurement; read-only
│   ├── cmek-killswitch.sh      disables the key, proves the denial, restores in a trap
│   ├── teardown-kms.sh         staged: can a key ring actually be deleted?
│   └── validate.sh             every assertion against the cloud, not state
└── docs/                       figure plan, references, screenshots

# terraform/  two files, two stages, and the split is the experiment: the
#             central measurement needs one rotation to fire with nothing
#             subscribed to the topic.
# rotator/    ~50 lines. That its absence looks like an oversight rather
#             than a design is the week's whole point.
# scripts/    cmek-killswitch.sh degrades a control, so it restores it in a
#             trap — a failure midway must not leave the secret dark.
